# Keep the build context small and the layer cache stable.
#
# Everything here is either regenerated inside the image (node_modules, dist) or
# irrelevant to a build (logs, editor state). Shipping node_modules would also
# be wrong, not just slow: it holds platform-specific binaries built for the
# host, and Playwright's browsers must come from the image's own base.

node_modules
**/node_modules

dist
**/dist
build
**/build
coverage
**/coverage
.turbo
**/.turbo

# `*.tsbuildinfo` alone matches only the context root. These files sit next to
# each package's tsconfig (composite + incremental are on in tsconfig.base.json),
# so without the `**/` form they ride into the image, and tsc then believes every
# package is already emitted and skips emit — leaving dependents to fail with
# TS2307 on a package that just reported a successful build.
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Local environment and secrets never belong in an image.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

.runner-artifacts
playwright-report
test-results
*.log
**/*.log

# Docs and scratch files do not affect the build.
docs
README.md
.claude
